{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"article","sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"title":"Localization","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Empty\/Loading\/Error placeholders’ text — “Nothing Here,” “Loading,” “Retry,” “Something Went Wrong,” “Connection Issue” — comes from a String Catalog, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":", resolved from ScreenStates’ own bundle ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bundle.module"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than your app’s. That’s deliberate: a custom title your app passes in (see below) is never run back through localization, and a language you add to "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"your own"}]},{"type":"text","text":" app’s catalog has no effect on these five strings — they only ever resolve against ScreenStates’ bundle. English, Spanish, French, and Russian are built in today."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Adding-a-language-to-ScreenStates","text":"Adding a language to ScreenStates"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is a change to the package itself, not something a consuming app can do on its own — it needs a PR. Open ","type":"text"},{"code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and add a ","type":"text"},{"code":"localizations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entry for the new language code under each of the five string keys:"}]},{"syntax":"json","type":"codeListing","code":["\"Retry\" : {","  \"comment\" : \"Title of the button that retries loading after an error.\",","  \"localizations\" : {","    \"en\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Retry\" } },","    \"de\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Wiederholen\" } }","  }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every one of the five keys needs an entry for every language — a string present in English but missing a translation elsewhere fails CI (see below). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStatesStrings.swift"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s doc comments list all five keys and their English text if you’re starting from scratch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Overriding-text-per-app","type":"heading","text":"Overriding text per-app","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You don’t need a new language, or a PR, to show different text than the built-in default — two options, depending on how much you want to replace:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" takes a ","type":"text"},{"code":"title","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directly, bypassing ","type":"text"},{"code":"Localizable.xcstrings","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entirely for that one string. Pass your own localized string (from your own app’s String Catalog, ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSLocalizedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whatever) instead of the default:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title: String(localized: \"No Results\"))"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has no equivalent for its title or Retry button text today — only the error’s own message is customizable, via ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For anything else — the Error placeholder’s title, the Retry button’s text, or any text at all in a shape the built-in views don’t expose a parameter for — pass a fully custom placeholder instead of the default one, via ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","type":"reference"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":" builder closures (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"‘s equivalent. A custom placeholder can still reuse "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" so VoiceOver announces transitions with the same wording your custom text uses, instead of the default’s."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/localization"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Localization"},"abstract":[{"text":"How the default placeholders’ built-in text is localized, how to add a language, and how to show different text instead without touching ScreenStates itself.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/Accessibility":{"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/accessibility","kind":"article","title":"Accessibility","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Everything the default placeholders — and your own custom ones — get for free: VoiceOver, Reduce Motion, Increase Contrast, Dynamic Type, and stable identifiers for XCUITest.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateDisplayableError":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Lets an error type supply its own user-facing message, distinct from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizedDescription"},{"type":"text","text":" — which is often a debugging string (or, for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Error"},{"type":"text","text":" with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomStringConvertible"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizedError"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conformance, just the type name) rather than something to put in front"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the person using the app."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatedisplayableerror","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","title":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"tex